1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,920
Solitude is not a private therapeutic place.

2
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:26,760
Rather, it is the place of conversion.

3
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:37,320
It is the place where the old self dies and the new self is born.

4
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:45,720
Solitude is the furnace of transformation.

5
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:52,360
Without solitude, we remain victims of our society and continue to be entangled in the

6
00:00:52,360 --> 00:01:00,920
illusion of the false self.

7
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:06,920
Solitude is the place of the great struggle and the great encounter.

8
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:17,480
So wonderful to see all of you today.

9
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:19,480
If we haven't met yet, my name is Ryan.

10
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:21,480
I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

11
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:27,000
I want to echo Andy's sentiment to those of you that are new or newer, whether you are maybe

12
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
a spiritual seeker, skeptic, or maybe you left the church for a while and are coming back.

13
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
We work really hard to be a safe place for people to explore faith, where real people

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,360
with real lives can learn how to follow Jesus in community with one another.

15
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:47,560
We are by no means perfect, but that's kind of what we're all about here.

16
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:51,000
And so if that's something that you're interested in, please find somebody in the lobby after.

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,280
Find me.

18
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:57,560
We'd love to talk to you and find out how you can get more connected here at our church.

19
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:01,160
We have been in a series on solitude, as you can see.

20
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,680
This is week three of four weeks.

21
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:09,400
And the solitude series is in a larger series about what we call practice-based discipleship.

22
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:14,120
And practice-based discipleship is really about offering our entire selves to God

23
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:17,080
so that he can transform us into people of Christ-like love.

24
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:22,440
Much of American Christianity often focuses on the mind and the heart.

25
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:28,920
But if you read the teachings of Jesus, he is constantly engaging the whole person.

26
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:35,640
And he isn't just wanting us to agree intellectually with his teachings, his moral ideology,

27
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:41,800
but he's actually inviting us to follow him, to do the things that he did, to become like

28
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:47,240
the person that he was so that we can share the love of God with the world all around us.

29
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:53,160
And we believe, I believe personally, that solitude is particularly important in our current moment

30
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:55,560
of busyness and distraction.

31
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:59,160
Our lives are filled with busyness and distraction.

32
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:03,960
And it could be easy for us to go throughout the entire day without even thinking about the reality

33
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:06,120
that there is a God who made us and loves us.

34
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:14,520
And so solitude is this invitation to set aside time where we become aware of God's radical love for us.

35
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:20,360
This series, actually, we intentionally planned it leading into the season of Lent,

36
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:26,680
which if you don't come from a church that practices the church calendar, that's fine.

37
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,400
I didn't either.

38
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:32,680
But Lent is a season where we're invited to intentionally go into the desert with God,

39
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:37,840
to fast from certain things, to set aside certain comforts and pleasures

40
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:42,140
in order to allow ourselves to experience God's presence in fresh ways.

41
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:46,800
And just like solitude, Lent teaches us by taking things away from us.

42
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:51,680
And so love for you to make plans to join us for that Ash Wednesday service.

43
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,740
If that's something that you've never experienced before,

44
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:59,160
we will try and make it as like the smallest amount of weird as possible.

45
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:05,440
It will end with me putting ashes on your forehead and telling you that you are going to die one day.

46
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,940
So that, it will be weird.

47
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:10,960
But as normal as possible, we will try.

48
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:15,260
So just to recap where we've been in solitude, and then we'll hop into today's message.

49
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:21,360
Week one, we define solitude as a space that we create for God free from all other inputs or agendas.

50
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:27,720
Many of us have quiet time with the Lord, where we set aside time free from inputs, but we come to God with agendas.

51
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:33,360
We come to God with what we want to learn, the questions we want to ask, the prayers we want him to answer in solitude.

52
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:38,180
Although that is a good thing, solitude is this additional step where not only are we removing our inputs,

53
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:44,540
but we're removing our agendas, and we're just giving him space to speak to us, allowing him to work in our lives.

54
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,760
So that's what solitude is.

55
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:50,560
And then Nick last week said that solitude is a place where we allow the dust to settle in our lives,

56
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:54,740
and we end up encountering ourselves as individuals on a deeper level.

57
00:04:54,740 --> 00:05:02,040
We understand the shame, the guilt, the regret, the fear, all of the emotions that are buried deep down inside of us,

58
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,980
and we offer them to God so that he can transform us,

59
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:08,960
so that he can heal the deepest, darkest wounds inside of ourselves.

60
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:14,280
Solitude is a space that we create for God to allow ourselves to feel who we are

61
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:14,920
in light of him.

62
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:17,020
It's the Genesis, naked and unashamed.

63
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:20,260
Nick said last week, which I love the line,

64
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:23,580
how often do we come before God hiding with fig leaves?

65
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:29,540
We are back in the Garden of Eden, and solitude is a place where we can remove the fig leaves,

66
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:35,640
be naked before God, and allow him to remind us that we are loved no matter how much we've fallen short,

67
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:39,400
no matter how much we've run away from him, that we are loved by him.

68
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:43,880
Today, we are going to talk about how solitude is a place where we,

69
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,720
often encounter God's enemy.

70
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,680
Exciting, right?

71
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:49,680
Why would we do that?

72
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:52,760
Why are we creating a space to encounter God's enemy?

73
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,440
That doesn't seem very church-like.

74
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:57,900
We have a green room meet, or we have a meeting with the band before service,

75
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:59,360
so we put our hands in like a team.

76
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,240
We always come up with a word to break on.

77
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,960
And I was like, wow, we're talking about Satan today.

78
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:05,900
I don't think we can say Satan on three.

79
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:11,860
So, that's kind of the roadmap for where we're at.

80
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:15,880
Hopefully, it'll make sense in a few minutes, but just track with me if that's okay.

81
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:16,360
Sound good?

82
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,280
All right, let's pray, and we'll do it.

83
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:24,560
Father in heaven, we are so grateful for yet another opportunity to be in this place with these people,

84
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,380
with your spirit.

85
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:33,140
We pray that you would just be at work the way in which you do through your spirit

86
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:36,360
in the lives of each one of us in this room, God, that we would hear from you,

87
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:40,340
that you would allow us to hear what we need to hear,

88
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:42,940
to be drawn into your presence,

89
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:46,240
to be drawn out of the busyness and distractions of our lives,

90
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,360
and to hear from you, God, speak to us.

91
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,040
I echo April's prayer.

92
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:55,440
May not a single person in this room walk away not having heard from you.

93
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:58,300
God, do what only you can do.

94
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:01,100
In Jesus' name I pray.

95
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:01,900
Amen.

96
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:06,140
If you have a Bible, if you carry a physical Bible with you,

97
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:09,040
which I would encourage all of you to do, I think that's a great idea.

98
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,420
We're going to be in Matthew chapter 4.

99
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:15,340
If you're new to the Bible, Matthew is the first book of the New Testament,

100
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:18,540
so if you flip to the middle, turn right, about 100 or 200 pages,

101
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:19,880
you should run into the New Testament,

102
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,380
and Matthew should be easy to find from there.

103
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,400
Matthew chapter 4 will be our main text.

104
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,420
We'll get there in a little bit.

105
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:31,700
In 1820, Thomas Jefferson created what is now known as the Jefferson Bible.

106
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:37,360
By taking the Bible and literally, with a razor blade and a stick of glue,

107
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:43,760
cutting and pasting numerous sections of the New Testament that he called his extractions of the doctrines of Jesus,

108
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:48,540
which got me thinking, I wonder if I could take a book that I like,

109
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:52,780
cut some of it out, and republish it as my own work,

110
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:56,140
and get some royalties, because I could use a little bit of extra cash.

111
00:07:56,140 --> 00:08:00,240
No, so this is what Thomas Jefferson did.

112
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:03,520
This process included, literally, him removing all of the miracles of Jesus,

113
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:06,800
most of the mentions of anything spiritual, including the resurrection.

114
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:10,480
Now, I want to be careful here, because some of you in here,

115
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:13,840
as skeptics or as people who are just spiritually seeking,

116
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,620
you might resonate with Jefferson's approach.

117
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:18,900
Many people like the teachings and moral examples of Jesus,

118
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:22,540
but can't get down with him casting out demons or raising people from the dead.

119
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:24,760
That's a fine starting point.

120
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,000
It's okay to start there.

121
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,940
If you're here and that's where you're at, I don't mean to insult you with this,

122
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:33,160
but my guess is the majority of us in the room have likely come to know

123
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:36,820
that you cannot have the true Jesus without the supernatural.

124
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:42,280
Some of us might laugh at the naivety of Thomas Jefferson's approach,

125
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:46,220
and some of us might be appalled at the heretical nature of such an action.

126
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:53,720
But what if many of us in this room are functionally doing the same thing as Thomas Jefferson,

127
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:57,480
except instead of using a literal razor blade and a stick of glue,

128
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:01,620
what if we have framed our theology in such a way that explains away

129
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:04,100
the supernatural elements of the Scriptures?

130
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:09,400
We wouldn't pull out a literal razor blade or a stick of glue,

131
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:13,660
but we've created this theology that allows us to downplay

132
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:16,180
some of the supernatural things in the Scriptures.

133
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:21,560
I came across a blog this week from a seminary student who was struggling with this.

134
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:26,600
He was at a highly intellectual seminary, constantly framing theology,

135
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:30,180
inspecting the word of God, and building these structures of theology,

136
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:34,040
and he was frustrated with the fact that most of the theology he was learning

137
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,140
ignored or explained away the supernatural.

138
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:36,800
And he wrote this.

139
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:37,580
I found it powerful.

140
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,700
He said,

141
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:42,780
Western Christians cannot help but be impacted by the culture around us.

142
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:46,680
We have gone along with our culture's dismissal of the supernatural realm.

143
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:51,840
Out of the fear that we will offend other people, lose a seat at the table of public discourse,

144
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:54,080
or be written off as weird.

145
00:09:54,080 --> 00:10:00,960
We often read the Bible as if every passage dealing with demons, angels, or supernatural healings have been blotted out.

146
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:10,620
Blinded in this manner, we try and follow Jesus, help others, and solve the world's problem with only one partial picture of reality.

147
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,240
I don't know about you, but this has often been my experience.

148
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:20,440
I've often ignored or explained away things that are hard to digest in our current Western cultural moments,

149
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:24,740
so that I don't lose a seat at the table, so that people don't think I'm nuts.

150
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:33,880
Is it possible that not only our Western theology, but also our avoidance of solitude,

151
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:41,140
allows us to ignore the very real presence of the spiritual enemies of God that seek to influence our lives?

152
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:45,960
C.S. Lewis wrote a great piece that many of you are probably familiar with called The Screwtape Letters.

153
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:55,500
This fascinating fiction was about how he saw Satan and demons working against God's presence and purpose in people's lives and in culture.

154
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:57,740
It's beautiful.

155
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:58,600
It's powerful.

156
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:02,040
However, many of us don't consider this possibility much at all.

157
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:09,880
And, equal opportunity offender in the room, some of us go way too far on the other side of the thing.

158
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:12,840
Anything that bad happens to us is Satan or the demon's fault.

159
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,560
We stub our toe.

160
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,120
We're like, devil's in here.

161
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:18,580
All right, let's slow our roll a little bit, right?

162
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:25,840
Let's have a balanced approach where we engage with and have space for the spiritual and supernatural,

163
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:29,420
and yet don't make everything that happens to us totally that.

164
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:35,540
As we dive into Matthew 4, I think we will see that solitude isn't just a space we create for God,

165
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:43,840
but it is a space where we can become aware of the enemy's relentless pursuit to distract you from God's calling on your life

166
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:46,760
and to deceive you into living for lesser things.

167
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:53,440
So, if you want to keep pretending that spiritual realities don't exist or that everything bad is demonic,

168
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,520
then avoid solitude.

169
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:59,680
But if you want to receive clarity about how the enemy is at work to distract and deceive you

170
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:03,920
away from the abundant life that Jesus offers you and towards destruction and chaos,

171
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:07,540
then I'd encourage you to lean into this practice of solitude.

172
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:12,340
If you have a bulletin and you're a type A person, you want to follow along with the notes,

173
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:14,660
there are some notes on the back, and this is my main thesis.

174
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:19,460
My main point for the rest of our time together is that solitude is a training ground

175
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:23,000
for battle against distraction and deception of the enemy.

176
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:30,240
Solitude is a space that we create where we can become aware of how the enemy of God is seeking to distract us

177
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:37,400
and deceive us away from God's purposes and plans for our lives and towards lesser things.

178
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,720
So, let's read Matthew chapter 4.

179
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:45,240
We'll work through it verse by verse and unpack the rest of that definition with the rest of our time together.

180
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,680
Matthew chapter 4, verse 1.

181
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:52,960
This is right after Jesus was baptized, heading into the launch of his public ministry.

182
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:59,720
It says, then Jesus was led by the Spirit, the Spirit of God, led Jesus into the wilderness.

183
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,840
Remember, that's the word that we've been focusing on in this solitude series.

184
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,480
It's desert.

185
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,320
It's Oremus.

186
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:09,380
It's this solitary place where you can be totally alone from the distractions of this world.

187
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:14,920
Jesus was led by the Spirit into the Oremus to be tempted by the devil.

188
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,360
Is that weird to anybody but me?

189
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:32,620
Why on earth would the Spirit of God lead Jesus to a place where he was totally isolated and alone to be tempted by the very enemy of God?

190
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:41,880
Well, in order to unpack what's going on here, I think I have to give you the fastest and least nuanced overview of Satan and the demons of all time.

191
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:47,200
We've got to have some working theory for who Satan is and what's going on here.

192
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:52,960
So are we good for me to do that, knowing that I'm not giving you everything and I might fall short?

193
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:55,460
Let's listen fast, all right?

194
00:13:55,460 --> 00:14:00,740
We read at the very beginning of the Bible, in the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth.

195
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:05,780
We've talked about this in length not too long ago, that heaven is God's space.

196
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:07,860
Earth is human space.

197
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:15,740
They were meant to overlap, but at the fall, at sin, that there's been this separation between God's space and human space.

198
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:16,740
There's still overlap.

199
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:19,420
There's still, this is what we're talking about in the spiritual realm, right?

200
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:22,340
The spiritual realm is where heaven and earth overlap.

201
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:27,540
And the rest of the Genesis account is about how God created within the earthly realm.

202
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:34,640
That he created humans and animals and plants, and it gives us an explanation of all that he did in and with humanity.

203
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:42,440
However, the rest of the Bible gives us glimpses and clues that God didn't just create on earth, but he also created in heaven.

204
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:45,900
He didn't just create on our realm, but he also created in his realm.

205
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:52,780
And similar to how God created Adam and Eve to partner with him, stewarding the creation of earth, our space, for his purposes,

206
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:59,360
God also created divine beings to partner with him in the spiritual realm, to steward the heavenly realm.

207
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:04,320
God at his very core, and this is something we cannot miss, God at his very core is relational.

208
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:10,300
He is constantly creating and partnering with his creation in order to accomplish his purposes.

209
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:15,520
And that's why, as much as we might not like it, things often move so slow.

210
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:23,140
God's kingdom coming to earth moves at the pace of which we partner with and submit our lives in.

211
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:30,780
Just like Adam and Eve rebelled against God's good purposes on earth, they decide to take matters into their own hands.

212
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:36,400
They decide to steward God's creation their way rather than his way, and that leads us into chaos and destruction.

213
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:42,520
A number of divine beings made the similar decision in the heavens, in God's space.

214
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,320
These beings are referred to throughout the Bible as Satan and demons.

215
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:49,660
These are heavenly beings that were created by God to steward the heavenly realm with him.

216
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:54,420
And they, just like Adam and Eve rebelled against God on earth, they rebelled against God in heaven.

217
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:57,360
They began to work against God's purposes in the heavenly realm.

218
00:15:57,360 --> 00:16:01,780
Their sole purpose became the destruction of God's good world.

219
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:13,020
Since their rebellion, they have been working subtly behind the scenes to influence individuals and cultures away from God's purposes that lead to life and towards chaos and destruction.

220
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:17,980
The only thing they exist to do is to see God's purposes on earth, Lord.

221
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:29,480
Now, with all of that as our backdrop, why in the world would the Spirit of God lead Jesus into a solitude, what's the adjective there?

222
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:32,500
A solitary, thank you, Megan, that's wonderful.

223
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:43,620
Bonus points, a solitary place where he could expressly be tempted by the enemy who is seeking to destroy him at the very beginning of his public ministry.

224
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,500
There's two answers to that question.

225
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:56,360
One is a very big picture theological answer, which we will start with, and that is Jesus began his ministry by succeeding where all other human beings have failed.

226
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:07,720
Jesus, in the aremos, tempted by the devil, he becomes the new Adam who faces the same temptation that Adam and Eve faced in a garden full of luscious things.

227
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:13,120
Jesus is in the desert and faces the same temptation, and yet he succeeds where Adam and Eve fail.

228
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:25,640
This story of Jesus in the desert with Satan face to face, this is the beginning of Christ single-handedly dismantling the spiritual powers of darkness that will culminate in his sacrificial death and resurrection.

229
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:32,060
He begins his ministry by taking on Satan head-on to show what the rest of his ministry is going to look like.

230
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:40,900
I am going to single-handedly push back the powers of darkness that are trying to lead God's creation to destruction and chaos, and I will have the final victory.

231
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:44,040
I am preaching better than you all are responding.

232
00:17:47,540 --> 00:18:00,760
Jesus faces God's enemy head-on in the desert to prove that the rest of his ministry is going to be him single-handedly dismantling the powers and principalities that lead us to live for our own selves,

233
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:17,800
and he is going to culminate it with the sacrificial death on the cross, showing us that true power, that true abundant life, that the way we advance God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven is not by taking power and by manipulating it and using it to gain circles of influence,

234
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:22,380
but it's actually by laying down our power for our neighbors and for those who are in need.

235
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:27,020
This is what Jesus does.

236
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:32,980
The story in the desert is his first of many decisive blows that he will execute against our spiritual enemies.

237
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:34,900
The victory has been won.

238
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:37,120
The enemy is retreating.

239
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:38,720
Ultimate surrender is coming.

240
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:43,880
But that does not mean we get to do nothing, right?

241
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:47,580
We don't just get to sit back and wait and say, Jesus won on the cross.

242
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:52,960
He finished it all, and so we're just waiting for him to come back and do what he's going to do.

243
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,380
No, he invites us to partner with him.

244
00:18:55,380 --> 00:19:00,160
He gives us a blueprint for how we should live and surrender in relationship with him.

245
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:07,540
And I think, I will make the argument with the rest of our time, that him going into solitude is part of that blueprint,

246
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:16,320
that he's inviting us to follow him into solitude so that we can become aware of the enemy's temptation in our own life,

247
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:22,160
his deception, his distraction, and we can begin to push back against the power of the enemy in our life

248
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:24,900
and take ground for the kingdom of God.

249
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:32,160
Jesus went into the solitude to fight back against the distraction and deception of the enemy.

250
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:40,020
And if we choose to follow his example, it can become for us a training ground to battle against our spiritual enemy.

251
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:42,680
All right, let's unpack training ground, right?

252
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:51,820
Whenever I was taught this passage growing up, the emphasis was usually on how the enemy came to Jesus at his weakest point in life, right?

253
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:55,460
Forty days in the wilderness, fasting and praying.

254
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:58,780
Jesus was starving, exhausted, alone.

255
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,460
This is, isn't this like the enemy, right?

256
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:03,700
To come at Jesus at his weakest time.

257
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:08,900
But I have now come to believe that this is somewhat of a misguided reading of the text.

258
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,180
Yes, Jesus is physically tired.

259
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:17,600
He was starving, running on fumes, but he is at the height of his spiritual strength.

260
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:21,380
He just spent 40 days in solitude fasting and praying.

261
00:20:21,380 --> 00:20:27,860
He had gotten rid of all distraction, all earthly temptation in order to abide in the Father's love.

262
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:34,160
And I believe the enemy is actually approaching him when he is the most prepared to deal with temptations of the enemy.

263
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:40,120
A couple of years ago, I decided to train for a half marathon.

264
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:42,700
Any real marathoners in the room?

265
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,880
Some of you, a couple of you, right?

266
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,380
Like, I'm not that nuts.

267
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,880
But I'm a little nuts, right?

268
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:51,260
And so I was training for a half marathon.

269
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:58,680
And you might make the argument that before I ever began training for a half marathon,

270
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:02,240
that would be the time that I was most prepared to run a half marathon, right?

271
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:03,320
My legs are fresh.

272
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:08,680
Like, there's no, my body, I haven't put my body through this difficult regimen of training.

273
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:10,400
I haven't run all of these miles.

274
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,460
I got fresh legs.

275
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:12,480
I got food in my stomach.

276
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,060
I'm energized.

277
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:13,580
I'm ready.

278
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:14,560
Like, let's just go, right?

279
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,800
Why train when I'm good?

280
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:17,660
I'm good right now.

281
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:21,240
How do you all think that would work for me?

282
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:24,640
Not great, right?

283
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,420
Of course not.

284
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:31,460
It's at the end of the training, when you've put in hundreds of miles over weeks at a time,

285
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:34,280
that you are most prepared to run the race.

286
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:36,720
And I think that's what's happening here with Jesus.

287
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:42,120
He's spending time alone with God, apart from the distraction and the deception of the enemy.

288
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:46,980
He's preparing for this time of ministry when he is going to have to push back against the powers

289
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:52,920
and principalities of the spiritual realm in order to be fully obedient to his calling as Messiah.

290
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:56,840
And that's when the enemy comes to him.

291
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:57,420
He's ready.

292
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,120
He's prepared.

293
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:04,100
And I think in this story, Jesus gives us an example that solitude can become for us a training ground,

294
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:08,520
how we fight back against the distraction and the deception of the enemy in our life.

295
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:11,740
Don't worry.

296
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:16,000
I'm not going to invite you to go 40 days into the wilderness with no food.

297
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:20,680
But I do think that as we learn to implement this practice into our life,

298
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:26,460
as we increase time and regularity of spending alone time with God, free from all inputs and agendas,

299
00:22:26,460 --> 00:22:31,680
that we might begin to discern the areas in our life where the enemy is distracting us

300
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:35,460
and deceiving us from the abundant life that Jesus is inviting us into.

301
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:39,840
And if you're new to this practice, which most likely almost all of us are,

302
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:46,620
I want to remind us that just like me training for a marathon, I had to be half marathon.

303
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:47,780
See what I did there?

304
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:53,840
I tried to pull one on you guys and make it seem like I was more than I am.

305
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:54,140
Nope.

306
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,120
Half marathon.

307
00:22:55,120 --> 00:22:59,920
Just like that, when you start training for something you've never prepared for,

308
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,040
you're going to have to be willing to suck it first.

309
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:04,760
Right?

310
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:09,400
Like, I had to be willing to like be gassed at the end of a mile and a half

311
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:12,560
in order to get to a place where I was ready for 13.1.

312
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:13,900
And the same is true with solitude.

313
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:19,080
If you have been brave enough over the last two weeks to try this practice of solitude,

314
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:21,880
you've likely found that it is far harder than you might have thought.

315
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:25,460
And you don't seem like you're gaining traction at all.

316
00:23:25,460 --> 00:23:30,160
I would just encourage you, keep going, keep pressing in.

317
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,560
You'll have to be willing to suck it first.

318
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:32,460
It's a training ground.

319
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:34,580
It's something that we have to work at and build up towards.

320
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:40,080
Not only is it a training ground, but it's a training ground to fight back against distraction.

321
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:41,940
The enemy is sneaky.

322
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:43,680
The Bible calls him the father of lies.

323
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:47,920
He would prefer to take us down passively so that we don't even know that he's doing it.

324
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:53,860
He'd prefer to distract us by the busyness of the noise of this world

325
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:56,760
that we don't even realize we're being pulled down a current

326
00:23:56,760 --> 00:24:00,200
that is leading us away from God's presence and purpose on our life.

327
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,300
I'd say it this way in the notes.

328
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:04,240
The devil doesn't have to deceive you if he can distract you.

329
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:12,800
There's a group from church history that learned this lesson long, long ago

330
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:17,460
and put down lots of writings that if you're a nerd and you want to get into, you can.

331
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:20,960
This group is called the Desert Fathers and Mothers.

332
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,220
They learned this lesson early.

333
00:24:22,220 --> 00:24:27,900
They formed around the third century as Christianity had moved from being a persecuted minority

334
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:30,140
to the official religion of the Roman Empire.

335
00:24:30,140 --> 00:24:36,240
See, it's hard to be distracted when your life is on the line every day.

336
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:43,060
When Christianity was a minority persecuted group, it was hard to lose focus on what you were living for

337
00:24:43,060 --> 00:24:45,340
when your life was at risk every single day.

338
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:50,060
But when it became more popular, when it became the culturally cool thing to do,

339
00:24:50,180 --> 00:24:53,980
which we still kind of have that a little bit in America today, right?

340
00:24:53,980 --> 00:25:01,140
It's easy for people to just become Christian, to just identify as Christian because that's what everybody else is doing.

341
00:25:01,140 --> 00:25:06,420
And that's what was happening when Christianity became the official religion of Rome

342
00:25:06,420 --> 00:25:09,680
is everybody was Christian, whether or not they were actually following Jesus,

343
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:14,280
whether or not they actually had a relationship with the living God.

344
00:25:14,280 --> 00:25:18,980
And the Desert Fathers and Mothers saw this and were afraid of what it was doing to their souls

345
00:25:18,980 --> 00:25:24,160
and said, we've got to get out of this cultural current that is just Christianity is just in the air

346
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:29,440
and we've got to get alone with God so that we can become aware of how we are being distracted

347
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:32,180
by the enemy of God to live for lesser things.

348
00:25:32,180 --> 00:25:35,760
And I think this is a lesson that many of us as American Christians can learn

349
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:40,780
because Christianity is just the air that we breathe in many parts of America still to this day.

350
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:45,620
It's the thing that we just identify with because our parents identified with it

351
00:25:45,620 --> 00:25:48,400
or because we grew up going to church every once in a while.

352
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,360
Like, yeah, I'm a Christian.

353
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:55,660
But it's this opportunity for us to withdraw and really consider,

354
00:25:55,660 --> 00:25:57,800
are we actually following Jesus?

355
00:25:57,800 --> 00:26:00,500
And where are there places in our lives where we're distracted

356
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:03,520
from actually doing the thing God's inviting us into?

357
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:07,460
So they retreated into the desert for intentional solitude and prayer

358
00:26:07,460 --> 00:26:11,240
to fight back against the enemy's distraction in their life.

359
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:13,720
In the furnace of their own spiritual training ground,

360
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:16,660
they began to write about what they called the unholy trinity,

361
00:26:16,660 --> 00:26:19,760
the world, the flesh, and the devil.

362
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:23,000
All three of these things constantly working against them

363
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:26,400
to live for lesser things than the thing that God had invited them into.

364
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:30,960
Will we learn from their example?

365
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:34,240
Will we take this practice of Jesus seriously?

366
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:38,580
I can almost guarantee that if we don't create space for God,

367
00:26:38,580 --> 00:26:40,060
free from all inputs and agendas,

368
00:26:40,060 --> 00:26:44,460
that we will in some ways be distracted by our own fleshly desires,

369
00:26:44,460 --> 00:26:47,240
by the cultural powers of this day, the world,

370
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:50,200
and by the enemy of God who is subtle and sneaky

371
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:54,420
and is just trying to get us to buy one lie at a time.

372
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:57,640
Jesus refused to be distracted.

373
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:59,660
He intentionally went into solitude

374
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:04,140
where he could become clearly aware of the deception of the enemy.

375
00:27:04,140 --> 00:27:08,920
All right, so let's look at what he becomes aware of,

376
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:12,580
this temptation of the enemy, starting in verse 2.

377
00:27:12,580 --> 00:27:13,440
It says,

378
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:16,980
After fasting 40 days and 40 nights, he was hungry.

379
00:27:16,980 --> 00:27:18,560
I love how honest the Bible is.

380
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:20,860
Fully God, fully man.

381
00:27:20,860 --> 00:27:23,300
Jesus is like, yeah, I need some food.

382
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:26,360
The tempter, the enemy, came to him and said,

383
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:29,620
If you are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread.

384
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:30,760
Jesus answered,

385
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:31,240
It is written,

386
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:33,280
Man shall not live on bread alone,

387
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:35,680
but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.

388
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,900
Then the devil took him to the holy city

389
00:27:37,900 --> 00:27:40,800
and had him stand on the highest point of the temple.

390
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,060
If you are the Son of God,

391
00:27:42,060 --> 00:27:42,360
he said,

392
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,520
Throw yourself down.

393
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:47,280
Now Satan is quoting Scripture to Jesus, which is fun.

394
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:49,240
So if somebody quotes Scripture to you and you're like,

395
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:50,240
Ah, it doesn't sound right.

396
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:51,160
It's okay.

397
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:52,840
Like, let's examine the claim here.

398
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,040
Because Satan says to Jesus,

399
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,140
He will command his angels concerning you.

400
00:27:56,140 --> 00:27:57,780
They will lift you up in their hands

401
00:27:57,780 --> 00:28:00,640
so that you will not strike a foot against the stone.

402
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:01,560
Jesus answered him,

403
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:02,560
It is also written,

404
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:04,420
Do not put the Lord your God to the test.

405
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:06,660
Again, the devil took him to a very high mountain

406
00:28:06,660 --> 00:28:09,640
and showed him all the kingdoms of this world and their splendor.

407
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,400
He said,

408
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:14,380
All of this I will give to you if you bow down and worship me.

409
00:28:14,380 --> 00:28:16,340
Jesus said to him,

410
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,920
Away from me, Satan, for it is written,

411
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:21,280
Worship the Lord your God and serve him only.

412
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:22,920
Then the devil left him.

413
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:24,280
I would emphasize and say,

414
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:24,940
Retreat it.

415
00:28:24,940 --> 00:28:27,460
And the angels came and attended to him.

416
00:28:27,460 --> 00:28:32,620
Jesus has this decisive victory won against the enemy.

417
00:28:32,620 --> 00:28:37,720
Fights back against three different deceptions from the enemy.

418
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:40,880
And although these three temptations are specific to Jesus

419
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:42,400
and his ministry as the Messiah,

420
00:28:42,400 --> 00:28:45,420
I think they represent three larger categories of lies

421
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:48,840
that the enemy is still using in our life today.

422
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:53,620
Again, if you're a type A note person, follow along.

423
00:28:53,620 --> 00:28:54,660
We've got them there on the notes.

424
00:28:54,660 --> 00:28:59,420
This first category of temptation that I think the enemy is using on Jesus

425
00:28:59,420 --> 00:29:01,340
that he's still using on us today is this.

426
00:29:01,340 --> 00:29:04,740
We can satisfy our desires apart from God.

427
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:07,740
Verses three and four.

428
00:29:07,740 --> 00:29:10,500
The tempter came to him.

429
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:10,740
He said,

430
00:29:10,740 --> 00:29:13,300
If you're the Son of God, take these stones and become bread.

431
00:29:13,300 --> 00:29:14,860
Jesus answered,

432
00:29:14,860 --> 00:29:15,320
It is written,

433
00:29:15,320 --> 00:29:16,700
Man shall not live on bread alone,

434
00:29:16,700 --> 00:29:18,740
but on every word that comes from the mouth of God.

435
00:29:18,740 --> 00:29:22,120
The enemy is trying to elevate Jesus' physical appetite

436
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:24,440
above all other things in his life.

437
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:26,660
This is the only thing that matters to you.

438
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:27,720
You have this appetite.

439
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:28,940
You have this need.

440
00:29:28,940 --> 00:29:30,540
You've been 40 days without food.

441
00:29:30,540 --> 00:29:31,600
You are the Son of God.

442
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:33,880
You can take this rock and you can make it food.

443
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:37,480
Even though the spirit is the one that led you out into the wilderness to fast and pray,

444
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,080
you can break the fast.

445
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:45,580
You can use your spiritual powers to give yourself the thing that you need most.

446
00:29:46,140 --> 00:29:51,300
The enemy is trying to get Jesus to elevate his physical appetite above his God-ordained purpose.

447
00:29:51,300 --> 00:29:57,160
And Jesus' response is that there is so much more to life than our physical appetites.

448
00:29:57,160 --> 00:30:02,720
And the enemy still uses this subtle lie in our lives today.

449
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:04,580
God created us with physical appetites.

450
00:30:04,580 --> 00:30:06,120
Surely they're meant to be satisfied.

451
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:11,460
The enemy wants us to take a good gift from God and make it ultimate.

452
00:30:14,060 --> 00:30:14,860
Think about it.

453
00:30:14,860 --> 00:30:20,560
In your life and in mine, our physical appetites often lead us to my physical appetites.

454
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:22,300
I'll take you guys off the table.

455
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:25,180
My physical appetites often lead me into gluttony.

456
00:30:25,180 --> 00:30:33,420
All right, now I'm going to put it back on us because I'm like, yeah, whoa, whoa, that's not me.

457
00:30:33,420 --> 00:30:33,800
All right.

458
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:38,660
Our physical appetites can often lead us to gluttony, drunkenness, addiction, and laziness.

459
00:30:38,660 --> 00:30:43,240
We turn to food and substance in times of distress

460
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:45,480
rather than into the loving arms of our Father.

461
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:50,620
The enemy takes a good gift from God and uses it to deceive us.

462
00:30:50,620 --> 00:30:52,180
Our physical appetites matter.

463
00:30:52,180 --> 00:30:53,460
These things are gifts from God.

464
00:30:53,460 --> 00:30:54,940
Food is a gift from God.

465
00:30:54,940 --> 00:30:56,740
Drink is a gift from God.

466
00:30:56,740 --> 00:30:59,420
These things are good and right, but when we make them ultimate,

467
00:30:59,420 --> 00:31:03,040
we end up running away from God's presence and purpose in our life.

468
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:07,200
Our sexual appetites lead us to lust, pornography, and infidelity.

469
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:12,000
The enemy takes a good gift from God and uses it to deceive us.

470
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:18,460
Our appetite for provision and for safety leads us to discontentment, greed, gambling, workaholism,

471
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:19,660
whatever it is for you.

472
00:31:19,660 --> 00:31:20,720
We have to have more.

473
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:21,640
We have to have more.

474
00:31:21,740 --> 00:31:26,260
It leads us to seek to find life and identity and provision.

475
00:31:26,260 --> 00:31:30,220
The enemy takes a good gift from God and uses it to deceive us.

476
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:33,660
Our appetite for approval, our appetite to be loved.

477
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:37,700
We were created to be in relationship with a loving God.

478
00:31:38,340 --> 00:31:41,940
We have this appetite for approval, but if we're not getting approval from God,

479
00:31:41,940 --> 00:31:48,280
it leads us to lie, to manipulate, and to gossip, to become religious, to put on a front,

480
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:52,900
to get whatever we can, to get false satisfaction out of other people,

481
00:31:52,900 --> 00:31:56,560
for them liking some version of ourself that we've created that isn't real.

482
00:31:58,580 --> 00:32:03,520
The enemy takes a good gift from God and uses it to deceive us.

483
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:11,480
These desires are meant to be fulfilled in relationship with God and in surrender.

484
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:15,140
This is what Jesus talks about, the abundant life, right?

485
00:32:15,140 --> 00:32:20,200
When we fulfill our desires in relationship with God, surrender to what he says is right,

486
00:32:20,200 --> 00:32:24,180
the lines that he draws as too much, it leads to abundant life.

487
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:29,840
But when we ignore his leadership in our life and we just take these appetites and run to fulfill them,

488
00:32:29,840 --> 00:32:33,420
it will ultimately lead us to death and destruction.

489
00:32:33,420 --> 00:32:38,320
Now, I know what some of you might be thinking.

490
00:32:38,320 --> 00:32:41,500
I always try and think about what you might be thinking when I'm writing my sermon.

491
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:44,440
Hopefully, it is what you're thinking.

492
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:47,960
If not, it's what an imaginary person in my head might be thinking.

493
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:54,240
This is all well and good, Ryan, but what does it have to do with solitude, right?

494
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:58,340
Like, solitude seems like this extra thing you just keep talking about you wanting us to do.

495
00:32:58,340 --> 00:33:02,500
How is this connected to the enemy's temptation in our life?

496
00:33:02,500 --> 00:33:09,260
Well, solitude, I believe, is a place where we can give God space to reveal these subtle lies of the enemy

497
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:12,300
that we are unknowingly believing.

498
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:20,680
I don't know about you, but I often come across people who have totally wrecked their lives by patterns of decisions that they've made.

499
00:33:20,680 --> 00:33:27,300
Oftentimes, they make most of these decisions in the dark until they can no longer conceal it, and then it comes to the light.

500
00:33:27,300 --> 00:33:32,600
And it's easy for me to look at these people and say, how did you get there?

501
00:33:33,320 --> 00:33:40,960
How did you allow the enemy to drape these chains of oppression over you that led you to destroy everything that you've worked built?

502
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:47,640
As I was thinking about that, I came across a sermon this week where the pastor said, you know, I thought about that a lot.

503
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:57,100
And the problem is the enemy doesn't come to us with a massive chain of bondage and slavery and oppression all at one time.

504
00:33:57,100 --> 00:34:04,540
He comes to us one link at a time, one little lie at a time in the darkness when no one's around,

505
00:34:04,540 --> 00:34:08,160
and it wouldn't affect anybody if I just said yes this one time.

506
00:34:08,220 --> 00:34:14,140
And before we know it, we fill our pockets, we fill our bags with one chain link at a time,

507
00:34:14,140 --> 00:34:19,600
and before we know it, we are buried under the weight of our decisions.

508
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:23,380
I love how Ian Simpkins puts it.

509
00:34:23,380 --> 00:34:28,120
He says, the choices we make today become the chains we wear tomorrow.

510
00:34:28,120 --> 00:34:35,820
And if we don't have a regular practice where we can get alone with God and just be honest

511
00:34:35,820 --> 00:34:42,300
and allow him to search our hearts and to reveal to us lies that we have been believing one chain at a time,

512
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:50,240
before we know it, we will be overwhelmed by our own choices.

513
00:34:50,240 --> 00:34:55,700
It will lead us to death and destruction rather than abundant life.

514
00:34:55,700 --> 00:34:57,060
That's why this matters.

515
00:34:57,060 --> 00:35:00,440
This is why solitude connects to these things because solitude gives us a place

516
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:04,120
where God can remove the distractions and the busyness of this world

517
00:35:04,120 --> 00:35:08,460
and help us pinpoint lies that we're believing that are ultimately leading us away

518
00:35:08,460 --> 00:35:10,460
from God's purpose and presence in our life.

519
00:35:10,460 --> 00:35:17,200
And it's way easier to readjust to course correct if we only have a handful of chains

520
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:19,580
that we have collected over time.

521
00:35:19,580 --> 00:35:22,360
And God can say, hey, let's get rid of those.

522
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:26,920
Let's repent and believe that I am who I say I am

523
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:32,020
and that if you surrender to me, your life will be led to the place you want it to go.

524
00:35:32,020 --> 00:35:33,780
Second temptation.

525
00:35:33,780 --> 00:35:36,920
We can define good and evil apart from God.

526
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:38,180
Verse five.

527
00:35:38,180 --> 00:35:42,840
The devil took Jesus to the holy city and had him stand on the highest point of the temple.

528
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:46,480
If you are the Son of God, he said, throw yourself down for it is written.

529
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:48,200
Remember Satan's quote in Scripture to Jesus.

530
00:35:48,200 --> 00:35:48,900
Love this.

531
00:35:49,540 --> 00:35:53,680
He will command his angels concerning you and they will lift you up in their hands

532
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:56,060
so that you will not strike your foot against the stone.

533
00:35:56,060 --> 00:35:57,200
Jesus answered him.

534
00:35:57,200 --> 00:35:58,160
It is also written.

535
00:35:58,160 --> 00:36:01,160
Do not put the Lord your God to the test.

536
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:05,580
The enemy takes a passage of Scripture that was written about the coming Messiah,

537
00:36:05,580 --> 00:36:08,360
that the Lord would not let him suffer,

538
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:11,500
that the Lord would not let him fall.

539
00:36:11,500 --> 00:36:15,320
And he says, look, you're at the beginning of your ministry.

540
00:36:15,780 --> 00:36:18,320
You're at the start where you're supposed to get popular.

541
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:21,040
People are supposed to know that you are the Son of God.

542
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:21,540
You're the Messiah.

543
00:36:21,540 --> 00:36:22,880
Let's skip all the suffering.

544
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:25,520
Let's skip all the daily faithfulness.

545
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:27,100
Let's skip all of the hard part.

546
00:36:27,100 --> 00:36:28,880
And why don't you just jump off of this temple

547
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:30,580
and some angels will come down and catch you

548
00:36:30,580 --> 00:36:34,680
and the entire city of Jerusalem will see that you are this promised Messiah.

549
00:36:34,680 --> 00:36:37,940
Let's skip the hard part and let's get to the part that you really want.

550
00:36:37,940 --> 00:36:43,100
See how this lie is saying like, no, like, yes, this is a truth from God

551
00:36:43,100 --> 00:36:45,520
and I'm going to twist it to benefit myself.

552
00:36:45,780 --> 00:36:51,820
Sound like anything we do today in our culture?

553
00:36:51,820 --> 00:36:57,540
The enemy wants us to take God's word and twist it to fit our own agendas.

554
00:36:57,540 --> 00:37:00,640
How often do we pick and choose verses in the Bible

555
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:03,220
that fit our convenient narrative about who God is

556
00:37:03,220 --> 00:37:04,640
and about how we should live?

557
00:37:04,640 --> 00:37:07,820
How often do we twist God's word and manipulate it

558
00:37:07,820 --> 00:37:10,520
to recreate a God in our own image and likeness,

559
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:13,300
essentially defining for ourselves what good and evil is

560
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:14,940
and justifying it with Bible verses?

561
00:37:14,940 --> 00:37:21,680
We use the Scriptures.

562
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:24,960
If we're not careful, the enemy can even take the Scriptures themselves

563
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:28,260
and help us to dig our heels in and justify behavior

564
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:29,900
that is not Christ-like love

565
00:37:29,900 --> 00:37:32,240
and we justify it with the Scriptures

566
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:35,740
because not because God is teaching us his word this way,

567
00:37:35,740 --> 00:37:38,220
but because the enemy is actually using God's word

568
00:37:38,220 --> 00:37:41,180
to allow us to redefine good and evil in our own image.

569
00:37:42,180 --> 00:37:44,980
And if we don't get alone with God in solitude

570
00:37:44,980 --> 00:37:49,640
and invite him to show us where we are believing the lies of the enemies,

571
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:53,580
we're not careful we'll end up creating a God that is in our own image.

572
00:37:53,580 --> 00:37:57,700
And solitude is a place where God can reveal to us the truth about himself

573
00:37:57,700 --> 00:38:07,520
and this is something that I have been working on for the last few years.

574
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:12,560
You grow up in the church, you go to Bible college,

575
00:38:12,560 --> 00:38:15,160
you get all of these ideas about God in your head,

576
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:21,080
you got all of these influences of people in your head that teach you what God is like,

577
00:38:21,500 --> 00:38:25,300
and then you go into ministry and you start reading the Bible for yourself.

578
00:38:25,300 --> 00:38:32,540
You start coming in contact with people's lives that don't fit your clean boxes of systematic theology.

579
00:38:32,540 --> 00:38:38,200
You're like, how do I make this work with this?

580
00:38:40,060 --> 00:38:47,000
And I think we just need to give God space in our lives to correct us, to challenge us,

581
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:52,360
to keep us from taking his word and manipulating it to fit our own agenda.

582
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:57,420
And it happens on all different sides of the spectrum for all different reasons and all different purposes.

583
00:38:57,420 --> 00:38:58,900
I'm not going to get into the specifics.

584
00:38:58,900 --> 00:39:01,680
You guys can probably think about it in your own head.

585
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:06,220
But this is a lie that the enemy is still using today to deceive us.

586
00:39:06,220 --> 00:39:11,720
He wants us to redefine God in our own image, to redefine good and evil apart from God.

587
00:39:11,720 --> 00:39:16,000
Solitude is a place where we can be made aware of these areas in our life.

588
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:20,700
Lastly, the last temptation of the enemy, I would put it this way,

589
00:39:20,700 --> 00:39:23,840
that we can have the life we were created for apart from God.

590
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:30,220
Again, the devil took him to the very high mountain and showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their splendor.

591
00:39:30,220 --> 00:39:32,560
All of this I will give to you, he said.

592
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:34,900
If you will bow down and worship me.

593
00:39:34,900 --> 00:39:39,040
Jesus said to him, Away from me, Satan, for it is written,

594
00:39:39,040 --> 00:39:43,340
Worship the Lord your God and serve him only.

595
00:39:43,340 --> 00:39:49,780
Satan comes right at the heart of Jesus' very purpose for being on earth.

596
00:39:49,780 --> 00:39:54,680
Jesus came to have victory over the powers and principalities of the earth,

597
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:56,400
to sit down at the right hand of the Father,

598
00:39:56,400 --> 00:40:01,180
having all of the kingdoms of this world under his leadership, under his footstool.

599
00:40:01,940 --> 00:40:03,540
Hebrews 1, 2 and 3 puts it this way.

600
00:40:03,540 --> 00:40:06,180
God promised everything to the Son as an inheritance.

601
00:40:06,180 --> 00:40:10,320
All the kingdoms of this world are Jesus' inheritance.

602
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:13,060
And through the Son, he created the universe.

603
00:40:13,060 --> 00:40:17,400
The Son radiates God's own glory and expresses the very character of God,

604
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:19,740
and he sustains everything by his mighty power.

605
00:40:20,620 --> 00:40:27,180
When he had cleansed us from our sins, he sat down in the place of honor at the right hand of the majestic God in heaven.

606
00:40:27,980 --> 00:40:33,420
This was the purpose for which Jesus was the Messiah,

607
00:40:33,420 --> 00:40:37,020
that he came to fight back against the powers and principalities of this world,

608
00:40:37,020 --> 00:40:40,280
so that he could have victory over the consequences of sin and death,

609
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:47,140
so that he could ultimately sit down in his rightful place as the king of the universe.

610
00:40:47,140 --> 00:40:47,860
And Satan is saying,

611
00:40:47,860 --> 00:40:55,300
you can have all of that or at least a watered-down version of that without going through the suffering,

612
00:40:55,300 --> 00:40:58,020
without going to the cross.

613
00:40:59,300 --> 00:41:01,680
I'll give you the thing that you were made for.

614
00:41:01,680 --> 00:41:05,760
I will give you the thing that you're here for.

615
00:41:05,760 --> 00:41:06,820
You can have it all.

616
00:41:06,820 --> 00:41:08,720
All you have to do is reject God.

617
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:10,720
No suffering, no crucifixion.

618
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:16,620
But Satan can only make this offer temporarily.

619
00:41:16,620 --> 00:41:21,620
Satan has power over the world today, but not forever.

620
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:28,940
And so he was offering Jesus something temporary that mimicked the life that he was created for,

621
00:41:28,940 --> 00:41:33,000
but fell woefully short of the life that he was here for.

622
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:40,400
The same lie is used by Satan for us today.

623
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:46,160
You can have all God's gifts without submitting to his rule or his reign in your life.

624
00:41:46,160 --> 00:41:49,840
You can take all of the gifts that God has offered you.

625
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,180
You can enjoy life.

626
00:41:52,300 --> 00:41:57,280
You can be the person God created you to be apart from God's presence in your life.

627
00:41:57,280 --> 00:42:00,780
And it'll work for a while.

628
00:42:00,780 --> 00:42:03,260
But it's temporary.

629
00:42:03,260 --> 00:42:05,840
And it ultimately leads to destruction.

630
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:11,760
I don't know about you, but this message has been hitting me really hard all week.

631
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:15,160
I'm often busy and overly distracted.

632
00:42:15,160 --> 00:42:22,160
I'm often lulled to sleep and spiritual irrelevancy through the distress.

633
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:34,020
Far more often than I'd like to admit, the guy with a Bible college degree still believes the subtle lies and deception that the enemy is selling me.

634
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:35,360
And my guess is I'm not alone.

635
00:42:35,360 --> 00:42:35,920
And my guess is I'm not alone.

636
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:44,740
So what if solitude became for us a training ground to battle against the distraction and deception of the enemy?

637
00:42:45,900 --> 00:42:52,560
What if we followed the example of Jesus confronted our enemy head on by the power of the Spirit in solitude?

638
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:57,300
What if we allowed the Spirit to lead us into the eremos, the solitary place?

639
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:10,160
To reveal to us the truth about ourselves, the lies that we're believing, the ways in which we're distracted, the ways in which we're living life for so much less than what God created us for.

640
00:43:11,120 --> 00:43:17,940
So I'd encourage you this week to try and carve out three periods of solitude sometime this week.

641
00:43:17,940 --> 00:43:25,380
I think all of us have three 10-minute blocks throughout the week that we can carve out to get alone with God apart from all inputs and agendas.

642
00:43:26,160 --> 00:43:32,320
And I just invite you to just come to this place with these three questions, one question at a time.

643
00:43:32,320 --> 00:43:37,040
First, where in my life am I elevating temporary pleasures above my eternal purpose?

644
00:43:37,040 --> 00:43:49,920
Where in my life is the enemy convincing me to sell myself short for who God made me to be in order to find satisfaction from the pleasures of this earth?

645
00:43:49,920 --> 00:43:55,840
Second, where in my life am I twisting God's definition of good to fit my own agenda?

646
00:43:56,160 --> 00:44:11,480
Where in my life am I doing the thing that I want to do and justifying it by twisting God to look like me rather than allowing the Holy Spirit to convict and to change me into His image?

647
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:19,680
And where, thirdly, where in my life am I content to have God's gifts apart from His presence and His leadership?

648
00:44:21,740 --> 00:44:30,520
Or in my life am I good to just enjoy life apart from the one who made me and has invited me into His presence?

649
00:44:30,520 --> 00:44:32,860
Let's pray.

650
00:44:32,860 --> 00:44:39,820
Father in heaven, thank you for Jesus

651
00:44:39,820 --> 00:44:46,820
who conquered the enemy head-on,

652
00:44:46,820 --> 00:44:49,100
who systematically

653
00:44:49,100 --> 00:44:58,540
pushed back the powers of darkness and principalities and the spiritual beings in the heavenly realm seeking to destroy us,

654
00:44:58,540 --> 00:45:01,420
who struck the final blow

655
00:45:01,420 --> 00:45:04,820
leading to ultimate victory.

656
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:11,800
God, may we lean into Your presence and walk in that very same victory.

657
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:22,800
May solitude become a place for us where we become aware of the distraction and the deception that the enemy wants to use against us

658
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:28,060
to lead us to a life that ultimately leads to chaos rather than the abundant life that Jesus invites us to.

659
00:45:28,060 --> 00:45:32,320
May we become partners with Jesus in His kingdom

660
00:45:32,320 --> 00:45:34,760
as we surrender to the truth.

661
00:45:34,760 --> 00:45:39,800
As we fight back against the

662
00:45:39,800 --> 00:45:42,800
currents of our culture that say

663
00:45:42,800 --> 00:45:45,740
you just have to do more, achieve more, accomplish more,

664
00:45:45,740 --> 00:45:47,120
and that we carve out space

665
00:45:47,120 --> 00:45:50,540
just to be used by You to love our neighbors as ourselves.

666
00:45:54,140 --> 00:45:56,760
Father, I pray that each person in this room this week

667
00:45:56,760 --> 00:45:58,980
would have an encounter with Your Spirit.

668
00:45:58,980 --> 00:46:06,140
And God, that You would do a work to conform them into Your image for Your glory.

669
00:46:06,140 --> 00:46:08,660
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

670
00:46:08,660 --> 00:46:09,960
Amen.

671
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:14,020
Go in peace, church.

672
00:46:14,020 --> 00:46:14,760
Amen.

673
00:46:14,760 --> 00:46:16,760
Amen.

674
00:46:14,760 --> 00:46:16,760
Amen.

675
00:46:44,020 --> 00:47:14,000
Thank you.

676
00:47:14,020 --> 00:47:44,000
Thank you.

677
00:47:44,020 --> 00:48:14,000
Thank you.
